    "created_at": "2026-09-18T13:26:24Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-09-18T13:26:24Z",
    "body": "Closing per the discussion in #12496: as @rakina noted, the spec already behaves this way. Nothing in the bfcache/navigation text changes a document's focused area or invokes the focusing/unfocusing steps, and the focus fixup rule only runs for fully active documents. The existing note is just a clarification of that, so no normative change is needed.\n\nThe motivating Chromium fix has landed and is on by default (https://crrev.com/c/7829940), aligning with WebKit and passing the existing WPT (html/browsers/browsing-the-web/back-forward-cache/focus.html).\n\nSorry for potentially wasting your time, I am new to the spec game. Thanks for the guidance!",
